  "Start with an empty list `[]`, loop over something, and `append` the items you want to keep or the values you calculate. It's the accumulator pattern for lists.",
  "evens = []\nfor n in range(1, 11):\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        evens.append(n)\nprint(evens)    # [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\n\nsquares = []\nfor n in range(4):\n    squares.append(n * n)\nprint(squares)  # [0, 1, 4, 9]",
